  "scope": "# Review: ec9cf2c80d58 conflicted-return reconciliation\nTask/source: `ec9cf2c80d58` generator `4.1.0`; generator SHA-256 `39cb6a9ff704cbc37689246fc0a7f2cd40a6b95de37ea6fb94fa20e8947413e9`; canonical `RULE_HASH` `899eb4e6a25d`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: the owner privacy correction hashed only inputs, so distinct visible demonstration labels could receive the same public ID; IDs now hash the exact visible bytes through the shared helper.\nMerged value: retained the reviewer-authored two-policy Python/Racket prototype and the owner-authored private-field masking, then added exact per-challenge public files, duplicate-visible-payload rejection, and four distinct queries per episode.\nCompatibility: both historical three-demo/one-query episode prefixes remain byte-for-byte unchanged; the production generator and canonical rule were not edited.\nChecks: 74 task tests passed; live Racket matched 14/14 stored labels; all 8 queries distinguish the opposite policy; the bounded public/private adversarial probe passed.\nSupplementary tickets: the pinned audit replay reproduced 9/15 rotated-holdout warnings without clearing the audit; the blind NVARC prediction failed and the file was assessed ambiguous because orange-hit reflections were absent from pairs 0\u20133.\nRemaining limits: two declared settings, two retained evidence episodes, finite seeds, and no production/catalog/training approval.\nReference-rule changes: none.\nDisposition: routine, ready to integrate as a task-local prototype/test/documentation delta.\n\n## Reconciled implementation",
